<% layout("/layouts/boilerplate") %>
<article class="legal-page">
  <span class="wander-eyebrow">WANDERSITE · YOUR INFORMATION</span>
  <h1>Privacy notice</h1>
  <p class="legal-updated">Last updated: 1 November 2026</p>
  <p>WanderSite is a hotel and stay discovery website with member accounts and community-submitted listings. This notice explains the information used to operate those features.</p>

  <h2>Information you provide</h2>
  <p>When you create an account, WanderSite stores your username and email address. Authentication credentials are handled through Passport Local Mongoose and are stored as password hashes, not plain-text passwords. When you use member features, the service also stores the stays you save, listings you submit, and reviews you write.</p>

  <h2>Images and listing content</h2>
  <p>Images uploaded for member-created listings are processed through Cloudinary, the configured image-hosting provider. Do not upload photographs or personal information that you do not have permission to share.</p>

  <h2>Sessions and hosting</h2>
  <p>WanderSite uses a session cookie to keep you signed in. Session records are stored in MongoDB Atlas through the application's session store. The application is hosted on Render. These providers process technical information as needed to operate the service.</p>

  <h2>Maps and external services</h2>
  <p>Map tiles are provided by OpenStreetMap, and the site may load fonts, interface libraries and images from third-party content delivery networks. Your browser may contact those providers directly and share ordinary request metadata such as your IP address.</p>

  <h2>Hotel information and bookings</h2>
  <p>Editorial hotel profiles are discovery information. WanderSite does not currently collect payment details, process reservations, or verify live room rates and availability. When you open an external hotel search or third-party site, that site's privacy policy applies to your activity there.</p>

  <h2>How information is used</h2>
  <p>Information is used to authenticate members, remember saved stays, display listings and reviews, secure the service, and keep the application operating. We do not display private account credentials on public hotel profiles.</p>

  <h2>Your choices</h2>
  <p>You can remove stays from your saved list. You can manage content you have submitted through the available account features. To request help with account information, use the support or contact channel provided by the site operator.</p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>This notice may be updated when the site's features or service providers change. The updated date above indicates the latest revision.</p>
</article>
